course: dictionary
lesson: 7204
title: pH and the ph sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: pH is a number that shows how acidic or alkaline a liquid is. The pH scale runs from 0 to 14. «The pH scale runs from 0 to 14.» Pure water sits in the middle at 7.
explain: Below 7 means acid, such as lemon juice at about 2. Exactly 7 is neutral. Above 7 means alkali, such as soap at about 9 to 10. The stronger the acid, the lower the number.
explain: Scientists can read pH from a colour. Red cabbage juice changes shape and colour at different pH levels. Litmus paper and universal indicator change colour too, so you can match the colour to the pH number.
explain: In spelling, the letters «ph» together make an /f/ sound, as in phone and elephant. Many words with ph come from Greek. So when you see ph, it is a clue that the sound is /f/, not /p/ and /h/ separately.
fact: pH is a number from 0 to 14 that shows how acidic or alkaline a liquid is.
fact: Pure water is pH 7, which is neutral.
fact: Lemon juice is about pH 2, so it is an acid.
fact: Bleach is about pH 12 to 13, so it is an alkali.
fact: The letters «ph» usually make an /f/ sound, as in «phone» and «elephant».
exercise: «Pure water is pH 7.» What does pH 7 mean? | Strong acid | Lemon juice | Strong alkali | *Neutral
exercise: «Lemon juice is about pH 2.» Is lemon juice an acid or an alkali? | *Acid | Alkali | Soap | Neutral
exercise: Which letters make the /f/ sound in «phone»? | *ph | on | ho | pn
test: «Soap is about pH 9 to 10.» Is soap an acid, neutral or alkali? | Acid | Pure water | Neutral | *Alkali
test: Which word has the /f/ sound spelled with ph? | *photo | fog | fox | fan
exam: «Milk is close to neutral, just below 7.» Which pH is milk closest to? | pH 0 | pH 14 | pH 12 | *pH 6
